docs {
  # Batch Download ZIP Stream

  **Method:** `POST`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/attachments/batch/download`
  **Auth:** Required (Bearer Token)

  ## Description

  Streams a compressed `.zip` archive on the fly containing all requested attachments. The server streams files directly from RustFS into the zip stream without accumulating the whole archive in server RAM.

  ## Request

  ### Headers

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`) |
  | `Content-Type` | `string` | Yes | `application/json` |

  ### Body

  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `attachment_ids` | `int64[]` | Yes | List of attachment IDs to include in the ZIP (max 50) |
  | `zip_filename` | `string` | No | Custom filename for the zip archive (defaults to `attachments.zip`) |

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**
  ```http
  Content-Type: application/zip
  Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="attachments.zip"
  <binary zip stream>
  ```

  ## Errors

  * `400 Bad Request` — Empty attachment IDs list or exceeds limit of 50 items
  * `401 Unauthorized` — Missing or invalid token
  * `403 Forbidden` — Access denied to one or more attachments
  * `404 Not Found` — No files found to include in the zip archive
}
